Colton,

Yes, the mean shape is the consensus shape from gpagen. The shape residuals, by definition, do not include the mean shape, so while they encode patterns of shape variation, they do not allow (easily) a visualization of those differences. The mean shape must be included.

As to your other question: that is a longer answer and is question-specific. We can take that off-line to the extent I can do so.

